flowchart TD
    P["<b>Prompt</b><br/>Janet's ducks lay 16 eggs per day. She eats 3<br/>and bakes muffins with 4. She sells the rest<br/>for $2 each. How much does she make daily?"]

    VLLM["<b>vLLM Server</b> (remote HTTP)<br/>Hosts copy of <b>LLM to train</b> (Qwen2.5-1.5B / 7B)<br/>Generates G=4 rollouts + <b>old_log_probs</b> per token"]
    P --> VLLM

    ROLLOUTS["<b>Rollouts</b><br/>1: '16−3−4=9, 9×2=18'<br/>2: '9 eggs left, $18'<br/>3: '16×2=$32'<br/>4: '16−3=13, $26'"]
    VLLM --> ROLLOUTS

    ENV["<b>Environment Service</b> (HTTP)<br/>Binary check: does final number = 18?<br/>Rewards: [1.0, 1.0, 0.0, 0.0]"]
    ROLLOUTS --> ENV

    GRPO["<b>GRPO Advantages</b><br/>A_i = (r_i − mean) / std<br/>[+0.87, +0.87, −0.87, −0.87]"]
    ENV --> GRPO

    ACTOR["<b>Actor Forward Pass</b> (FSDP)<br/>Computes <b>new_log_probs</b> per token"]
    ROLLOUTS --> ACTOR

    RATIO["<b>Per-Token Importance Ratio</b><br/>ratio = exp(new_lp − old_lp)"]
    ACTOR -->|new_log_probs| RATIO
    VLLM -.->|old_log_probs| RATIO

    CLIP["<b>PPO Clipping</b> (per-token)<br/>−min(ratio × A, clamp(ratio, 0.8, 1.2) × A)"]
    RATIO --> CLIP
    GRPO --> CLIP

    KL["<b>KL Penalty</b> (per-token, Schulman)<br/>(ratio − 1) − log(ratio)"]
    RATIO --> KL

    TOTAL["<b>Total Loss</b><br/>mean(policy_loss) + kl_coef × mean(KL)<br/>averaged over tokens, then sequences"]
    CLIP --> TOTAL
    KL --> TOTAL

    GRAD["<b>Gradient Step</b><br/>clip_grad_norm → optimizer.step()"]
    TOTAL --> GRAD

    SYNC["<b>Sync Weights → vLLM</b><br/>HTTP POST (every 3 steps)"]
    GRAD --> SYNC
    SYNC -.-> VLLM

